  "description": "The tree is a silver birch with three trunks and the circumference of each of these trunks is 55-59 cms.I estimate the height to be 24 feet. Some branches were blown off this winter and very few remain.The tree stands at the back of the rear garden, some four feet forward from the back wall. Work to construct a garden studio took place in 2020 and we installed a pump to ensure water could reach the tree. The tree did not flourish and we finally had to accept the fact that it had died. My husband's terminal illness and his death in August 2025 has delayed me attending to this issue, and I apologise.",
